Sam: Of course! I''ve been fascinated by the Maya since I was little.
Lily: Me too. I really want to see one of those huge stone pyramids.
Sam: I''m more interested in their calendar. They tracked the stars so carefully.
Lily: That''s amazing. Our guide says the writing on the walls still can''t be fully read.
Sam: I know. No one has worked out every sign yet. It''s a real mystery.
Lily: Let''s bring notebooks and write down whatever the guide tells us.
Sam: Good idea. I can''t wait to set out!', 'Lily 说班级下月要去参观玛雅遗址,问 Sam 去不去;Sam 当然去,从小就着迷玛雅;Lily 最想看巨大的石头金字塔;Sam 更感兴趣他们的历法和观星;导游说墙上的文字至今无法完全读懂;两人决定带笔记本,记下导游讲的内容。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where is the class planning to go?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To the Maya ruins.","To the South Pole.","To a deep-sea museum.","To a space centre."]},{"q":"What does Lily most want to see?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["An old shipwreck.","A huge stone pyramid.","A modern factory.","A coral reef."]},{"q":"What is Sam most interested in?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The Maya calendar and their study of the stars.","The price of the tickets.","The local food.","The weather that day."]},{"q":"What does the guide say about the wall writing?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It was written last year.","It still cannot be fully read.","It is very easy to understand.","It has all been removed."]},{"q":"What do they decide to bring?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A small boat.","Warm winter coats.","Notebooks to write down what the guide says.","A large telescope."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Using only their eyes, they followed the movements of the stars and planets.
From this knowledge they built a calendar of great accuracy.
It lost only a few seconds each year, which is amazing for ancient times.
They did all of this without any of the machines we use today.', '玛雅人是了不起的观天者;仅凭肉眼追踪星辰和行星的运动;由此建立了极为精确的历法;每年只差几秒,这在古代令人惊叹;而这一切都没有借助我们今天使用的任何机器。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What were the Maya remarkable at?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Building ships.","Growing rice.","Painting walls.","Watching the sky."]},{"q":"How did they follow the stars?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Using only their eyes.","Using modern telescopes.","Using computers.","Using radios."]},{"q":"What did they build from this knowledge?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A large pyramid of gold.","A very accurate calendar.","A deep canal.","A fast sailing ship."]},{"q":"How accurate was the calendar?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It was wrong by a whole month.","It changed every single day.","It lost only a few seconds a year.","It was never finished."]},{"q":"What did they manage without?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Any sunlight.","Any people.","Any water.","Any modern machines."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Jack: The book says there wasn''t just one reason. Several causes worked together.
Emma: Right. As the population grew, they needed much more land for farming.
Jack: So they cut down a lot of the forest. That may have harmed the land.
Emma: And then there were the droughts. The rains failed for years.
Jack: With less rain, the crops failed and food ran short.
Emma: No wonder the people finally left their homes.
Jack: Whatever the exact cause, the great cities slowly fell into ruin.', 'Emma 和 Jack 讨论历史题:玛雅城市为何被弃;Jack 说书上讲并非单一原因,多个原因共同作用;人口增长需要更多农田;于是砍掉大量森林,可能损害了土地;接着又有连年干旱、雨水不至;雨水减少导致作物歉收、粮食短缺;人们最终离开家园;无论确切原因如何,伟大的城市慢慢沦为废墟。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the history question about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Why the Maya cities were abandoned.","How to build a pyramid.","Where to find coral.","When the calendar was made."]},{"q":"According to Jack, how many causes were there?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only one clear cause.","Several causes acting together.","No causes at all.","Exactly two causes."]},{"q":"Why did the people need more land?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Because they loved travelling.","Because the sea was rising.","Because the population was growing.","Because they had no homes."]},{"q":"What happened when the rains failed?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The cities grew much larger.","The forests quickly returned.","The calendar stopped working.","Crops failed and food ran short."]},{"q":"What finally happened to the great cities?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They slowly fell into ruin.","They were rebuilt in gold.","They moved to the coast.","They were never affected."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Each one shows people trying to reach the edges of their world.
Yet today we have better maps of the Moon than of our own sea bed.
Only now are we learning to deal with the cold, darkness and pressure of great depths.
Much of the deep ocean is still waiting to be explored.', '海洋之下约有三百万艘沉船;每一艘都展现着人类努力抵达世界边缘;然而今天我们对月球的地图比对自家海床的还要详尽;直到现在我们才开始学会应对深海的寒冷、黑暗与压力;深海的大部分仍在等待被探索。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"About how many shipwrecks lie beneath the oceans?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["About three hundred.","About three million.","Only two or three.","None at all."]},{"q":"What does each shipwreck show?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["People who hated the sea.","Modern fishing boats.","People trying to reach the edges of their world.","Empty metal containers."]},{"q":"What do we have better maps of than the sea bed?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Our own gardens.","The city centre.","Ancient pyramids.","The Moon."]},{"q":"What are we only now learning to deal with?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The cold, darkness and pressure of the depths.","The heat of the desert.","The noise of the city.","The light of the stars."]},{"q":"What is true about much of the deep ocean?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It has all been mapped.","It is still waiting to be explored.","It is completely empty.","It is too shallow to study."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Dr Reed: Simple curiosity. I just can''t stop wondering what lies beyond the next hill.
Host: But aren''t you ever afraid of the unknown?
Dr Reed: Of course. The trick is to subdue that fear and keep going.
Host: Many people would rather steer clear of such danger.
Dr Reed: True. But I always think twice and study the risks before I set out.
Host: So courage isn''t the same as rushing in blindly?
Dr Reed: Exactly. A wise explorer looks into things carefully first.', '主持人问 Reed 博士是什么驱使她探险;她说只是纯粹的好奇,总忍不住想知道下一座山后面有什么;主持人问她难道不怕未知;她说当然怕,关键是克制恐惧、继续前进;很多人宁愿避开这种危险;但她出发前总会三思并研究风险;主持人问勇气是否等同于盲目冲入;她说正是如此,明智的探险者会先仔细调查。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Dr Reed say drives her exploring?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A wish to be rich.","A love of comfort.","Simple curiosity.","A fear of home."]},{"q":"How does she handle her fear of the unknown?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["She gives up at once.","She ignores all danger.","She never feels any fear.","She subdues it and keeps going."]},{"q":"What would many people rather do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Steer clear of such danger.","Follow her everywhere.","Explore even more wildly.","Live in the jungle."]},{"q":"What does she do before she sets out?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She rushes in without any planning.","She thinks twice and studies the risks.","She forgets about the dangers.","She asks no questions at all."]},{"q":"What does Dr Reed say a wise explorer does?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Acts blindly and very fast.","Avoids all new places.","Looks into things carefully first.","Travels without any aim."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U5', 'fltrp');
It led our ancestors to discover fire and to cross unknown seas.
When you face something strange, you do not always have to run away.
Take a careful look, think it over, and you may learn something new.
Whatever you discover, the courage to explore is always worth it.', '纵观历史,好奇心一直推动人类前进;它引领我们的祖先发现火、跨越未知的海洋;当你面对陌生事物时,不必总是逃开;仔细看一看、好好想一想,你也许会学到新东西;无论你发现什么,勇于探索永远值得。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What has pushed humankind forward through history?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Fear.","Laziness.","Silence.","Curiosity."]},{"q":"What did curiosity lead our ancestors to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Discover fire and cross unknown seas.","Stay in one place forever.","Stop asking any questions.","Avoid all kinds of travel."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say you do not always have to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Take a careful look.","Run away from something strange.","Learn something new.","Be brave and curious."]},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest you do instead?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Shout as loudly as you can.","Close your eyes tightly.","Take a careful look and think it over.","Forget about it at once."]},{"q":"According to the speaker, what is always worth it?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The money you save.","The time you waste.","The fear you feel.","The courage to explore."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U5', 'fltrp');

